      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8rd",
          "text": "Slip and Fall Back Pain Symptoms",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b8rl",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l8ri",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "/common-back-injuries-after-a-fall/"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8rf",
          "text": "Back pain is one of the most commonly reported ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8rg",
          "text": "symptoms of slip-and-fall injuries",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8rh",
          "text": ", and it can range from mild discomfort to debilitating pain. A fall might cause a simple muscle strain or something more serious, like a herniated disc or spinal fracture. The range of ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8rj",
          "text": "common back injuries after a fall",
          "marks": [
            "l8ri"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8rk",
          "text": " runs from strains and sprains to compression fractures and spinal cord trauma, and these injuries can affect your ability to work, sleep, or even walk comfortably.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b8rn",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8rm",
          "text": "In some cases, pain might radiate down the legs, indicating potential nerve damage or spinal involvement. If your symptoms persist or worsen after a fall in Colorado, seeking prompt medical attention is crucial. Delaying treatment could not only jeopardize your health, it may also weaken your legal case if you decide to pursue compensation under the state’s premises liability laws.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b8rp",
      "style": "h3",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8ro",
          "text": "Can Slip-and-Fall Accidents Be Deadly?",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b8ru",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8rq",
          "text": "Yes, in certain situations, a slip and fall can lead to fatal outcomes.",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8rr",
          "text": " Older adults, in particular, are more susceptible to complications such as hip fractures, internal bleeding, or traumatic brain injuries. Falls can also aggravate pre-existing conditions, further compromising a person’s health. Even if a fall seems minor, it can result in life-threatening consequences depending on the individual’s age and health. According to the National Safety Council, falls are a leading cause of preventable injury-related deaths, particularly among older adults and workers in high-risk environments. These incidents may also cause long-term disabilities that impact quality of life and independence.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b8rw",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8rv",
          "text": "The Role of Common Injuries in a Slip and Fall Case",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b8ry",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8rx",
          "text": "The type and severity of injuries sustained in a fall can significantly affect a legal claim. More serious injuries tend to result in higher medical expenses, longer recovery periods, and greater emotional distress. In a personal injury case, the documentation of symptoms and treatment is essential in proving the extent of physical harm, the financial consequences, such as medical bills and lost income, and the non-economic toll, including ongoing pain and emotional suffering. Clear medical records, witness testimony, and a prompt diagnosis all help support the strength and credibility of your case.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b8s0",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8rz",
          "text": "Can You Sue Someone for a Slip and Fall Injury?",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b8s6",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "l8s3",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "/what-are-compensatory-damages/"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8s1",
          "text": "In many situations, you may sue someone if their negligence led to the fall.",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8s2",
          "text": " Property owners in Colorado have a ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8s4",
          "text": "legal duty",
          "marks": [
            "l8s3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8s5",
          "text": " to maintain safe premises. If they fail to remove hazards like wet floors, icy walkways, or broken handrails, they may be held liable for resulting injuries.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b8s8",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8s7",
          "text": "However, proving fault requires establishing several key elements. The property must have a dangerous condition, and evidence should show that the property owner knew or reasonably should have known about it. Additionally, it must be clear that they failed to take reasonable steps to correct the hazard or provide adequate warning to visitors.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b8sa",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8s9",
          "text": "Consulting with a law firm can help determine if your situation qualifies under Colorado’s premises liability laws.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b8sc",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8sb",
          "text": "When to Seek Medical Attention After a Fall",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b8se",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8sd",
          "text": "Prompt medical care is crucial after a slip and fall, even if you believe the injury is minor. Some injuries may not show symptoms immediately, but a medical exam can reveal hidden issues before they worsen.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b8sg",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8sf",
          "text": "A healthcare provider can evaluate your condition through physical exams, imaging tests, and other diagnostics. This protects your health and creates essential documentation that may support a legal case, especially if complications arise later or symptoms evolve over time.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b8si",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8sh",
          "text": "Contact Our Colorado Slip and Fall Injury Attorneys",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b8so",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8sj",
          "text": "At ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8sk",
          "text": "Dormer Harpring",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8sl",
          "text": ", we help people across Colorado hurt in slip-and-fall accidents understand their rights. Whether it happened in public, at a business, or on private property, we know how overwhelming the aftermath can be. If you or a loved one is suffering from ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8sm",
          "text": "slip-and-fall injury symptoms",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s8sn",
          "text": ", don’t wait to get help.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b8st",
